<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Caracciolo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1752–1799</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Caracciolo was a Neapolitan admiral who commanded the navy of the Parthenopean Republic in 1799. Having served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> king, he joined the republic and fought royalist and British ships in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Bay of Naples</a>. After the republic's fall he was tried by a royalist court-martial aboard Nelson's flagship and hanged from the yardarm of the frigate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minerva">Minerva</a> on 29 June 1799, an execution that damaged Nelson's reputation.</p></div>
